  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Tue Jun 2 2026\n\nThe entire region will finally see a break in the humidity today\nas drier air filters into the region following the passage of a\ncold front. High pressure over the Great Lakes and Midwest will\nbring dry conditions to the region today through Friday. H5\nridging will be positioned over the region as well, and thermal\nprofiles look to be near typical early June values. Therefore, \ntemperatures will be near normal values. \n\nBy this weekend, the ridging over the region will become \nsuppressed by deepening troughing over the central Great Plains.\nA surface cold front will attempt to move into the region\nSaturday into early next week. Model guidance is not in good\nagreement whether the front will actually clear the region, but\nit will be close enough to trigger isolated to scattered storms\neach day from Saturday through Monday. Additionally, increasing\nGulf moisture ahead of the front will bring a return of\nnoticeable humidity levels.",
